course: dictionary
lesson: 6139
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Military is an adjective, and it means having to do with soldiers, the army, the navy, the air force, or war. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «Letters, video calls and a calendar help when a parent works far away or is deployed (sent away to work) in the military.» The clues are deployed and works far away, so the military here means the armed forces, the people who serve a country as soldiers.
explain: Look for clue words. In «military base», «military uniform» and «military parade», the second word tells you the subject is soldiers. A base is where soldiers live and train, and a uniform is what they wear. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases use military in a special way, so read the whole phrase. «Military time» is the 24-hour clock, so 15:00 means three in the afternoon. «Military precision» means very exact. A «private military contractor» is a hired soldier, also called a mercenary.
fact: Military means having to do with soldiers, the army, the navy, the air force, or war.
fact: The military is a country's armed forces, so it can also be a noun.
fact: A «military base» is a place where soldiers live and train.
fact: «Military time» is the 24-hour clock: 15:00 means three in the afternoon.
fact: «Military precision» means very exact, as when everything is done perfectly on time.
exercise: «Letters, video calls and a calendar help when a parent works far away in the military.» What does military most likely mean here? | A kind of school | A type of car | A short holiday | *The armed forces of a country
exercise: A sign says «military time» and shows 15:00. What time is it? | *Three in the afternoon | Fifteen minutes past three | Three in the morning | Half past five
exercise: A «private military contractor» is a hired soldier. What is another name for one? | A teacher | A baker | A pilot's friend | *A mercenary
test: What does «military precision» mean? | *Very exact | Very old | Very wet | Very loud
test: «The Ada programming language was created first for the US military.» Which group was it first made for? | Shops and banks | *The armed forces | Farmers and fishers | Schools and hospitals
exam: Jayden says «military» always means war. Is he right? | No, it always means a type of car | *No, it can also mean soldiers, the army, or the 24-hour clock in military time | Yes, but only in history books | Yes, it always means war
